# ==============================================================================
# Runtime & Session State
# ==============================================================================
# Runtime state. Yours, not the project's.
# Commit it deliberately if you want testing history to travel with the repository —
# but read it first: evidence excerpts can contain data from whatever you tested.
# Ignore the CONTENTS, not the directory -- git cannot un-ignore a file inside an
# ignored directory, so `state/` plus `!state/README.md` would silently drop the README.
state/*
!state/README.md
demo-state/
*.state

# ==============================================================================
# Environment Variables & Secrets (Never commit secrets to GitHub)
# ==============================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
*.crt
*.pfx
*.p12
credentials.json
service-account*.json
token.json
*.token

